OL,3,CJersey and Guernsey record hottest
OL,4,Cmonth for third time in a row
OL,6,FIn Jersey, July 2026 was its hottest
OL,7,Fmonth on record - with temperature
OL,8,Ffigures dating back to 1894.
OL,10,FThe island saw less than half its
OL,11,Fexpected rainfall, which mostly fell
OL,12,Fduring one three-hour period on
OL,13,FWednesday 15 July.
OL,15,FGuernsey saw even less rain - just
OL,16,F12.5% of the average expected for July
OL,17,F- with records starting in 1843.
OL,19,FMeasurable rainfall on the island was
OL,20,Fonly recorded on three days.
